# res://dialogue/chapter_launch.dialogue
# Launch monologues shown over the portal swirl, one title per chapter, plus the return
# monologue played on the way back to the hub.
# Speaker-less on purpose: conversationballoon.gd hides the nameplate entirely when
# dialogue_line.character is empty.

~ university_2
You're here now.
Swirling.
Floating.
# step 2.392: the dream's music starts with the swirl and plays on into chapter2_intro.dialogue, where it
# cuts out as Fiona wakes up. step 2.397: the portal's hum carries the first three lines alone, then fades
# as the music takes over here. to start the haunt on another line, move these two lines together.
do SoundManager.fade_out_portal_hum(3.0)
do SoundManager.play_music_track("haunted_techno", 3.0)
Going back to who you once were.
What will your first memory reveal to you?
Whose face will you see first?
Will it be the face of someone you loved?
Or the face of someone you hated?
Hate...
Now, that's a strong emotion.
Let's start at the beginning.
=> END

~ university_2_replay
# step 2.419: a REPLAY of Keeping Busy (the chapter has been finished once). draft lines: rewrite freely, keep the
# title. the two "do" lines match ~ university_2: the dream's music has to be playing when chapter2_intro starts.
do SoundManager.fade_out_portal_hum(3.0)
do SoundManager.play_music_track("haunted_techno", 3.0)
You've been here before.
You know how this one ends.
Go on. Look around. Try the other door.
It won't change a thing.
It already happened.
=> END

