~ layla_runs_away
# step 2.413: the launch monologue for "Layla Runs Away"
Layla.
You remember Layla now, don't you?
She... was clearly important enough to you for you to have this memory.
A day spent working together.
An invite for coffee.
Who knows what it could lead to... right?
Just... remember one thing about Layla.
In the beginning of fall, when you lo-
Oh, wait, what?
Never mind.
You have arrived.
Have fun.
=> END

~ layla_runs_away_replay
# step 2.419: a REPLAY of Layla Runs Away. draft lines: rewrite freely, keep the title.
Layla, again.
You've turned this one over before.
Nothing in it is going to move.
But it's a nice one to sit in.
=> END

~ return_to_hub
Fading out.
You're back.
Back to your reality.
Who's gonna pay your bills?
Who are you?
Is anyone... out there thinking about you?
=> END

~ layla_runs_away_return
# step 2.423: the exit monologue of "Layla Runs Away", under black after its conversation
Ah.
Looking back, it all makes sense.
The girl was flustered at the thought of your naked body.
What about you, though?
What were you feeling then?
What are you feeling... now?
=> END

~ build_end_note
# step 2.421: shown once, the first time the memory box is closed after Keeping Busy is finished. an out-of-world
# note from the developer, so nobody goes looking for new scenes in the hospital. speaker-less on purpose.
# draft lines: rewrite freely, keep the title.
A note from the developer:
This is where the story stops for this build. The hospital stays as it is for now.
The memories stay open. Go back into them whenever you like, and keep an eye out for anything the insurance form might want.
Thanks for playing. More soon.
=> END